{"step_index":124,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-05T18:55:31Z","content":"Here is the exact step-by-step guide to run the commands in your Windows terminal:\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Open Terminal (PowerShell or Command Prompt)**\n\n1. Press **`Win + R`** on your keyboard (or click the Windows Start menu).\n2. Type **`powershell`** (or **`cmd`**) and press **Enter**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Navigate to the Project Folder**\n\nCopy and paste this command into your terminal window, then press **Enter**:\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Start the Application**\n\nRun the launcher script by typing:\n\n```powershell\n.\\run-app.bat\n```\n\n*(If you are in standard Command Prompt `cmd.exe`, you can simply type `run-app.bat` and press Enter).*\n\n---\n\n### **Alternative: Run Directly with Maven in PowerShell**\n\nIf you prefer to run the raw commands directly without the `.bat` script, paste these 3 lines into PowerShell:\n\n```powershell\n$env:JAVA_HOME = \"C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\jdk-17.0.10+7\"\n$env:PATH = \"$env:JAVA_HOME\\bin;C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\tools\\apache-maven-3.9.6\\bin;$env:PATH\"\nmvn spring-boot:run\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Verify It Is Running & Open in Browser**\n\n1. Watch the terminal output. Within a few seconds you will see:\n   ```text\n   Tomcat started on port 8080 (http)\n   Started QualificationVerificationApplication in X.XXX seconds\n   Sample qualification data successfully seeded.\n   ```\n2. Open your browser and navigate to:\n   👉 **[http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080)**\n\n---\n\n### **Helpful Terminal Commands**\n\n- **To stop the running application**: Press **`Ctrl + C`** in the terminal window.\n- **To run all 26 automated unit/integration tests and check coverage**:\n  ```powershell\n  .\\run-tests.bat\n  ```","thinking":"The initial step is to detail the process of opening a terminal on Windows. It involves providing options: using `Win + R` followed by `powershell` or `cmd`, or searching the Start menu for \"PowerShell.\" This allows the user to prepare to execute the required commands. Afterwards, step-by-step copy-paste commands will be given to navigate the project directory.\n\n\n"}
