{"step_index":138,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-05T19:08:01Z","content":"Here is how to start the server inside **Visual Studio Code**:\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Open the Project Folder in VS Code**\n1. In VS Code, go to the top menu: **File** > **Open Folder...**\n2. Navigate to and select:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system\n   ```\n*(Opening this specific folder ensures VS Code recognizes `pom.xml` and the pre-configured settings).*\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Choose Any of These 3 Ways to Start the Server**\n\n#### **Method A: Using the VS Code Integrated Terminal (Easiest)**\n1. Open the VS Code terminal by pressing **``Ctrl + ` ``** (Ctrl + Backtick) or going to **Terminal** > **New Terminal**.\n2. Type:\n   ```powershell\n   .\\run-app.bat\n   ```\n3. Press **Enter**.\n\n---\n\n#### **Method B: Using VS Code Build / Run Task (Keyboard Shortcut)**\n1. Press **`Ctrl + Shift + B`** on your keyboard.\n2. Select **`Start Spring Boot Server`**.\n3. A terminal will automatically open and launch the server.\n\n---\n\n#### **Method C: Using VS Code \"Run & Debug\" (F5)**\n1. Press **`F5`** on your keyboard (or click the **Run & Debug** icon on the left sidebar).\n2. Select **\"Launch QVS Spring Boot Server\"** and click the green Play **(▷)** button.\n3. *Alternatively*, open [`QualificationVerificationApplication.java`](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/QualificationVerificationApplication.java) and click the **`Run`** button directly above the `main` method.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Open the Portal**\nOnce you see:\n```text\nStarted QualificationVerificationApplication in X.XXX seconds\n```\nOpen your browser and visit:\n👉 **[http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080)**\n\n---\n\n### **Summary of VS Code Shortcuts Configured for You**\n- **Start Server**: Press **`Ctrl + Shift + B`**\n- **Run All 26 Tests & JaCoCo Coverage**: Press **`Ctrl + Shift + P`** → type `Run Task` → select **`Run Automated Tests & JaCoCo`**","thinking":"To start the server, the project root directory must be opened in the development environment. This ensures the configuration files are accessible. The simplest approach involves using the integrated terminal within the development environment.\n\n\n"}
